{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception and motion capabilities, separating sensing (uncontrollable) and actuation (controllable) events. The specification encodes a safe, coverage-oriented supervisor: in clear states, random_walk is preferred for exploration, with occasional move_forward pulses for steady progress. Obstacle events trigger short, directed turn recoveries (CW or CCW) based on obstacle side, never enabling forward or random_walk in recovery. full_rotate is only enabled in a dedicated search state after repeated blockages. All states are total on uncontrollables, and only one controllable is enabled per state to avoid oscillations.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for sensing and actuation, with all events as specified.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe, deterministic exploration: random_walk in clear, move_forward for progress, directed turn recovery on obstacles, and rare full_rotate for last-resort scan."
  ],
